<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2970" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăpella</span></b> , ae, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The name of a Roman freedman</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				12, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 7, 25</span></i>; Planc. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The name of a credulous Jew who lived in the time of
				Horace;</i> hence, appellative for <i>a credulous
				man</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1, 5, 100</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>